<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="materialtypes">materialtypes</span></h2>
<p>The materialtypes worksheet defines the derived materials that can be assigned to an item. There can be multiple derived material types for each base material type, for example, both <b>Armor, Iron</b>, <b>Weapon, Gray Iron</b> and <b>Shield, Iron</b> (rows 1, 40 and 47 in materialtypes) are all derivatives of <b>Iron</b> (row 1 in materialrules).
</p><p>The original version of materialtypes released with the toolset contains several columns which are not required as they are redundant or contained in <b>materaialrules</b> (above). The only columns that are required are:
</p>
<ul><li> ID</li>
<li> Label</li>
<li> TINTFILE</li>
<li> Material</li>
<li> Sound_MatType</li></ul>
